---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="About | Crypto Yield Archive" description="Why Crypto Yield Archive exists and what it does not try to be.">
  <section class="panel hero-panel">
    <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
    <h1>About Crypto Yield Archive</h1>
    <p>Crypto Yield Archive is an evidence-based historical registry for crypto lending, Earn, and yield platforms.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="grid two-col" style="margin-top:18px;">
    <div class="detail-stack">
      <section class="panel card">
        <h2>What CYA is</h2>
        <p>CYA tracks what happened after users deposited assets into crypto yield platforms. It focuses on platform history, customer outcome, terms risk, failure chain, and supporting evidence.</p>
      </section>

      <section class="panel card">
        <h2>Why it exists</h2>
        <p>The 2021–2023 crypto lending collapse cycle produced many platform failures, withdrawal pauses, bankruptcies, restructurings, and unresolved customer outcomes. CYA keeps those histories in a structured registry instead of treating them as isolated news events.</p>
      </section>

      <section class="panel card">
        <h2>What CYA is not</h2>
        <p>CYA is not an APY ranking, yield discovery product, investment recommendation site, trading tool, or real-time TVL dashboard.</p>
      </section>

      <section class="panel card">
        <h2>How to read records</h2>
        <p>Each platform page should be read as a dossier: entity facts, timeline, customer outcome, terms risk, evidence, and uncertainty. A record can be useful even when the outcome is unknown, because unresolved status is part of the history.</p>
      </section>

      <section class="panel card">
        <h2>Corrections and source improvements</h2>
        <p>Good corrections include the platform name, the CYA page URL, the claim that appears wrong, one or more source links, and a short explanation. Official statements, court filings, bankruptcy documents, regulatory notices, and archived pages are preferred.</p>
      </section>
    </div>

    <aside class="panel card sticky-side">
      <h2>Quick links</h2>
      <div class="side-links">
        <a class="archive-link" href="/methodology/">Methodology</a>
        <a class="archive-link" href="/source-quality/">Source quality</a>
        <a class="archive-link" href="/timeline/">Timeline</a>
        <a class="archive-link" href="/outcomes/">Customer outcomes</a>
        <a class="archive-link" href="/stats/">Registry stats</a>
      </div>
      <h3 style="margin-top:18px;">Disclaimer</h3>
      <p>CYA is a historical and educational registry. It does not provide investment, legal, tax, or financial advice.</p>
    </aside>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
